From: eirikr <eirikr@localhost>
Date: 2026-05-13
Subject: [PATCH gnumach] ipc: raise ipc_kernel_map_size from 8 MB to 64 MB

The IPC kernel map (ipc_kernel_map) is the kernel virtual-memory region
used to back per-task port-name allocations during the
mach_port_names() RPC.  Each call to mach_port_names() temporarily
allocates a region from ipc_kernel_map sized to hold the task's name
table.

The current 8 MB cap (defined as a compile-time constant in
ipc/ipc_init.c) is exhausted on x86_64 systems during boot bursts of
fork/exec via run-parts and xargs.  On Debian GNU/Hurd 0.9, the
following message floods the console:

	no more room in ffffffffdff58888 (xargs(1838))
	no more room in ffffffffdff58888 (xargs(1838))
	[...]

Symptoms include init scripts hanging mid-boot and rc.local never
reaching its end, since each fork triggers a mach_port_names() copy
from the kernel-side ipc_kernel_map.

Raise the constant to 64 MB.  On the x86_64 port the kernel VA space
is large enough (canonical >>2 TiB) that this adds 56 MB of address
reservation without measurable cost: the submap is created via
kmem_submap which is lazily backed by physical pages on demand, so
the actual RSS only grows when the additional headroom is used.

Reproducing the bug pre-patch:

	# Boot debian-hurd-amd64.qcow2 under QEMU with QEMU_SMP=2 and
	# QEMU_RAM=2048.  Add a /etc/rc.local that runs `run-parts /etc/boot.d`
	# where /etc/boot.d/ contains 10+ shell scripts each spawning curl,
	# apt-get, grep, awk in pipelines.  Boot will hang around runlevel 2
	# with the "no more room" loop.

Post-patch the same workload runs to completion.

Reported-by: <iamhumanipromise1010101@gmail.com>
Suggested-by: Code-review of ipc/mach_port.c:mach_port_names
---
 ipc/ipc_init.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/ipc/ipc_init.c b/ipc/ipc_init.c
index 5dc7b5b..3a4f8b1 100644
--- a/ipc/ipc_init.c
+++ b/ipc/ipc_init.c
@@ -53,7 +53,7 @@

 static struct vm_map ipc_kernel_map_store;
 vm_map_t ipc_kernel_map = &ipc_kernel_map_store;
-const vm_size_t ipc_kernel_map_size = 8 * 1024 * 1024;
+const vm_size_t ipc_kernel_map_size = 64 * 1024 * 1024;

 /*
  *	Routine:	ipc_bootstrap
